WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:04.600
Although he's been a fixture in Hollywood
since his days on Saturday Night Live in the

00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:08.700
'80s, Eddie Murphy hasn't really done all
that much in the last handful of years.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.830
So where has he been?

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:10.900
And what has he been up to?

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.549
Here's a look at the real reason you don't
hear from Eddie Murphy anymore.

00:00:14.549 --> 00:00:15.799
This was all planned

00:00:15.799 --> 00:00:19.720
Although fans may be confused by Murphy's
recent absence from the big screen, the superstar

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:23.470
comedian has actually been laying the groundwork
for retirement for years.

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:29.080
"And I'm planning to make movies til I'm 50,
that's 2 years and 8 months, then I'm going,

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.320
then I'm going back to the stage."

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.010
Since then, Murphy has mostly lived up to
his word.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:38.930
His last major star vehicle, Tower Heist,
hit theaters a few months after his 50th birthday.

00:00:38.930 --> 00:00:45.000
He's since appeared in only two other movies:
the underwhelming A Thousand Words, in 2012;

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.309
and the very-low-profile indie Mr. Church,
which opened to mostly negative reviews in

00:00:50.309 --> 00:00:51.309
2016.

00:00:51.309 --> 00:00:55.210
Meanwhile, he did a bit of standup for the
first time in almost three decades while accepting

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:57.819
the Mark Twain Prize for American Humor in
2015.

00:00:57.819 --> 00:01:03.159
"Ya know they call it a prize, it's an award,
cause usually when there's a prize there's

00:01:03.159 --> 00:01:04.960
money involved."

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:09.620
(audience laughs)

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:13.480
"I thought I was gonna get some paper, I was
like 'Yooo'"

00:01:13.490 --> 00:01:15.250
Not interested in Hollywood

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.659
So why is Murphy basically retired?

00:01:17.659 --> 00:01:21.729
According to an interview with Rolling Stone,
it's simple: he's just happy with his life.

00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:25.969
"I only want to do what I really want to do,
otherwise I'm content to sit here and play

00:01:25.969 --> 00:01:27.260
my guitar all day.

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:31.240
I always tell people now that I'm a semiretired
gentleman of leisure, and occasionally I'll

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:33.149
go do some work to break the boredom up.

00:01:33.149 --> 00:01:35.100
… I'm chilling, no stress."

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.150
Sounds pretty awesome.

00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:39.460
From funny to flops

00:01:39.460 --> 00:01:43.380
Murphy's big-screen career has always been
a bit of a roller coaster, from highs like

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:47.840
Beverly Hills Cop to lows like The Adventures
of Pluto Nash, which remains one of Hollywood's

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:48.969
biggest failures.

00:01:48.969 --> 00:01:53.079
Still, the last decade has been especially
unkind to Murphy.

00:01:53.079 --> 00:01:58.729
In 2007 he starred in Norbit, for which he
"won" three Razzie Awards, and followed that

00:01:58.729 --> 00:02:04.360
up with a string of critical and box office
bombs, including Meet Dave, Imagine That,

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:06.250
and A Thousand Words.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:10.580
"Uh, uh, aahh, ahhhhh!

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:11.670
Aaaahhhhhhh!"

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:15.400
To his credit, Murphy has been a bit more
reflective in recent years, telling The Washington

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.930
Post that he was through taking roles just
for the money.

00:02:17.930 --> 00:02:20.510
"The check movies are over for me."

00:02:20.510 --> 00:02:21.849
Oscars snub

00:02:21.849 --> 00:02:26.030
Murphy made headlines in November 2011 when
he announced he would no longer be hosting

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:30.069
the 84th annual Academy Awards, set to air
the following February.

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:32.700
His decision didn't exactly come as a surprise.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:36.750
It was announced a day after that Brett Ratner,
the director of Tower Heist, had dropped out

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:41.849
as the telecast's producer after making anti-gay
remarks and discussing his sex life on Howard

00:02:41.849 --> 00:02:42.849
Stern.

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:46.600
Still, Murphy's decision to quit the Oscars
didn't sit well with everyone, especially

00:02:46.600 --> 00:02:48.349
among members of the Academy.

00:02:48.349 --> 00:02:52.390
One member told The Hollywood Reporter, "This
is like a big middle finger to the Academy

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:56.250
and to the industry," while another added,
"It was a career mistake.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.379
What the hell was he thinking?"

00:02:58.379 --> 00:03:00.220
Return to SNL

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:04.150
Murphy was one of many famous faces who took
part in Saturday Night Live's 40th anniversary

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:05.840
special in February 2015.

00:03:05.840 --> 00:03:10.590
But despite his high-profile appearance, Murphy
left many fans underwhelmed when he gave what

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:13.730
amounted to a barely one-minute speech.

00:03:13.730 --> 00:03:14.730
What kept him from doing more?

00:03:14.730 --> 00:03:18.580
"I will always love this show, and let's keep
on, let's have some more show let's have a

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:22.260
big round of applause to everybody."

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:27.150
According to the Washington Post, SNL wanted
him to play Bill Cosby, which didn't sit well

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:31.280
with Murphy at the time, given that Cosby
was facing accusations that he had sexually

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:33.659
assaulted dozens of women throughout his career.

00:03:33.659 --> 00:03:36.470
"I totally understood [why SNL wanted to do
it].

00:03:36.470 --> 00:03:38.280
It was the biggest thing in the news at the
time.

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:42.480
I can see why they thought it would be funny,
and the sketch that Norm [Macdonald] wrote

00:03:42.480 --> 00:03:43.480
was hysterical.

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:45.280
[But the story is] horrible.

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:46.480
There's nothing funny about it.

00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:49.750
If you get up there and you crack jokes about
him, you're just hurting people.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:50.750
You're hurting him.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:51.900
You're hurting his accusers.

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:56.069
I was like, 'Hey, I'm coming back to SNL for
the anniversary, I'm not turning my moment

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:58.269
on the show into this other thing.'"

00:03:58.269 --> 00:04:02.519
Ironically, Murphy wound up impersonating
Cosby while accepting his Mark Twain Award

00:04:02.519 --> 00:04:03.930
that October.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:14.810
"Some of the people, who feel that I should
give back my ------ ------- trophies!"

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:16.500
He expanded his family

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:20.199
Murphy's preference for being a chill dad
over a Hollywood megastar was confirmed in

00:04:20.199 --> 00:04:25.020
May 2016 when he and his girlfriend, Paige
Butcher, welcomed their first child together,

00:04:25.020 --> 00:04:26.210
Izzy Oona Murphy.

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:29.880
He clearly likes being a dad — he has eight
other children with four other women.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:33.710
But while he's enjoying new fatherhood once
again, there are limits even for him.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:34.900
"I don't change diapers."

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:35.900
"You don't?"

00:04:35.900 --> 00:04:36.900
"No.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:41.850
Cause I would be horrible at it, and that's
not fair to the child."

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.270
Projects in the works

00:04:43.270 --> 00:04:47.160
Although you may not see much of Murphy these
days, that doesn't necessarily mean he'll

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:48.450
be gone forever.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:52.449
In fact, the actor has a number of projects
in development, including a role playing Richard

00:04:52.449 --> 00:04:57.120
Pryor's father in the new movie for Lee Daniels
and the long-gestating fourth installment

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:59.169
in the Beverly Hills Cop franchise.

00:04:59.169 --> 00:05:03.360
Speaking to Ellen DeGeneres about the latter
project in 2013, Murphy revealed that he and

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:05.979
others were still fine-tuning the script.

00:05:05.979 --> 00:05:08.440
"If we can get the script just right it's
something that we'll do.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:12.080
But it has to perfect cause I don't wanna
do anything else that sucks."

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:12.620
"Ya."

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:13.320
"Ever again."

00:05:13.320 --> 00:05:16.020
(Laughs)

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:17.940
"That's a good goal, that's a really good
goal.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:20.020
I think most of us have that goal.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:21.020
Good, well, I hope-"

00:05:21.020 --> 00:05:23.470
"I don't wanna suck no more."

00:05:23.470 --> 00:05:24.630
Thanks for watching!

00:05:24.630 --> 00:05:27.410
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.629
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

